# Template for `.env.live`, which holds the live suite's stable credentials and is gitignored.
# Copy to `.env.live` and fill in. Never commit the filled file.
#
# CK_LIVE_API_KEY must be a **developer-environment** key: Preferences -> Advanced ->
# Manage API keys -> Generate new, on https://developer.clockify.me. The value is shown once.
# Confirm which environment a key belongs to before using it — a production key authenticates
# against api.clockify.me and is rejected 401 by the developer environment, and vice versa:
#
#   curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -H "X-Api-Key: <key>" https://developer.clockify.me/api/v1/user
#   curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -H "X-Api-Key: <key>" https://api.clockify.me/api/v1/user
#
# The live suite creates and deletes real time entries, so pointing it at production is a
# destructive mistake. A dev-only key cannot make it.
# CK_LIVE_WS is the sacrificial developer workspace — `69bda6b317a0c5babe34b4ff` at the time of
# writing (docs/13). Left blank here rather than pre-filled: a 24-hex value after `=` reads to a
# secret scanner as a credential, and this file is committed.
CK_LIVE_API_KEY=
CK_LIVE_WS=
CK_LIVE_API_BASE=https://developer.clockify.me/api

# Not stored here, and why:
#   CK_LIVE_ADDON_TOKEN     — decrypted from the installation record by scripts/live-env.sh
#   CK_LIVE_ADDON_BASE_URL  — a quick tunnel's hostname changes every start; pass it as $1
